PaymentRails_SweepNative
├── when caller is not the owner
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ZeroRecipient
├── given no native and no wrapped balance
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_ZeroNativeBalance
├── given the wrapper pays out less than the wrapped balance
│   └── it should revert with PaymentRails_UnwrapAmountMismatch
├── when recipient rejects
│   ├── it should revert with PaymentRails_NativeTransferFailed
│   └── it should leave both balances unchanged
├── given only native balance
│   ├── it should send the whole native balance
│   ├── it should return the amount sent
│   └── it should emit NativeSwept with recipient and amount
├── given only wrapped balance
│   ├── it should unwrap the whole wrapped balance
│   ├── it should not emit NativeReceived for the wrapper payout
│   └── it should send the unwrapped value
├── given both native and wrapped balance
│   ├── it should send the sum
│   └── it should drain paymentRails of both
├── when recipient re-enters wrapNative
│   ├── it should reject the re-entrant call as unauthorized
│   └── it should complete the sweep
├── given native ingress is disabled
│   └── it should sweep force-fed value
├── given value arrived without calling receive
│   └── it should include it
└── fuzz
    └── when native and wrapped balances are arbitrary
        └── it should deliver exactly their sum
